async ({ shell: { execFile, exec } }) => {
  const url = (await execFile("gh", ["pr", "create", "--base", "main", "--head", "chore/release-2.5.3", "--title", "chore: release 2.5.3", "--body", `Refs #85.

## Release notes

### Changed
- **The action sets up Node.js with \`actions/setup-node\` v7** (#85, changed in #86). When the runner has no Node.js 24 or later, the action installs it with \`actions/setup-node@v7\` instead of v6. You do not need to change your workflows. The examples in the docs now use \`actions/checkout@v7\` and pit v0.37.0. See [Workflows](https://github.com/cv/pi-action/blob/v2.5.3/docs/workflows.md).
